WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.380
Picture a shepherd at the end of the day,

2
00:00:02.430 --> 00:00:05.060
separating the sheep from the goats.

3
00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:09.960
In a parable of Jesus, all the nations
are judged by how they treated the hungry,

4
00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:12.300
the stranger and the prisoner.

5
00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:17.040
Yet the New Testament also says that
God desires all people to be saved.

6
00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:19.480
So will everyone be saved in the end?

7
00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:21.320
Or only some?

8
00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:24.320
In this mission, you'll meet
three Christian answers,

9
00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:28.200
from Augustine and Calvin
to Origen and John Hick.

10
00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:32.850
Then you'll see how each answer reads
the same parable in its own way.

11
00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:36.120
Your mission: work out the
three Christian answers,

12
00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:37.960
and the reasons behind each.
